 again before it was mended): EACH ITEM OF A LIST IS A UNIT OF ITS OWN IN THE
 SWEEP OF B1028'S TEST, AND B1222'S CORRECTION STANDS IN THE ITEM IT CORRECTS.

THE FINDING, MADE AGAIN on the test and on B1222's page. The sweep asks that the correction stand beside the zero it corrects, in the same unit. A list with no empty line between its items was one unit, so the correction in one item excused the zero stated in another. On B1222's page the correction stood as an item of its own, before the item it corrects, in a list the page counts as three counterexamples.

WHAT IS CHANGED. In the sweep each item of a list is a unit, with the lines that continue it. With that alone, the sweep reports one page on the tree: B1222's. There the correction is moved into the item it corrects, word for word, with a dated note that says it was moved; the list has three items again.

THE PLANTED CASES, in the patch's own test: a list whose first item carries the correction and whose third states the zero; and the list as it stood on B1222's page. Read as one unit, as it was, neither is reported; each is now. A twin, the correction inside the item, is not.

The test file: 10 pass. The reviewer's page is made again. 0 of 19.
